# Claim 1

An LED device, comprising:

a substrate having a mounting surface;

a plurality of LED units disposed on the mounting surface of the substrate, each LED unit comprising:

a light-emitting element having a first side surface and a second side surface opposite to the first side surface;

a plurality of first conductive connectors disposed on the first side surface, the plurality of first conductive connectors comprising n conductive connectors, wherein n is a positive integer;

a plurality of second conductive connectors disposed on the second side surface, the plurality of second conductive connectors comprising m conductive connectors, wherein m is a positive integer, and wherein n is not equal to m;

wherein each of the plurality of first conductive connectors and each of the plurality of second conductive connectors comprises a base portion connected to the light-emitting element and an extending portion extending outwardly from the base portion, the extending portion having a width that is asymmetric relative to a width of the base portion such that the extending portion extends further in a first lateral direction than in a second lateral direction opposite to the first lateral direction, thereby forming an asymmetrical shape of each of the plurality of first conductive connectors and each of the plurality of second conductive connectors; and

wherein the plurality of first conductive connectors and the plurality of second conductive connectors are electrically connected to a circuit layer on the mounting surface of the substrate to electrically connect the plurality of LED units.
